\section{Paper identifier helpers}

Scholar's internal paper identity uses DOI when available, otherwise a hash of
title + first author's last name (see \cref{ch:paper-identity}).

In practice, papers often transition from \enquote{no DOI} to \enquote{has DOI}
after enrichment or when another provider returns additional metadata.
That transition would change the paper's stable ID and could orphan existing
notes/decisions saved under the legacy hash ID.

To keep this backward compatible, we expose the legacy hash-ID algorithm and a
small arXiv helper that can derive the canonical arXiv DOI
[[10.48550/arXiv.<id>]] from arXiv URLs.

\subsection{Legacy hash IDs}

The legacy hash ID matches the [[Paper.id]] implementation for papers without
DOIs: SHA-256 of normalized title + first author's last name, truncated to 16
hex characters.

<<utils functions>>=
import hashlib
import re


def legacy_hash_paper_id(title: str, authors: list[str] | None = None) -> str:
    """Return the legacy hash-based paper id.

    This mirrors [[Paper.id]] for papers without a DOI. It is used to migrate
    persisted notes/decisions when a paper later gains a DOI.
    """
    if title is None:
        title = ""
    if authors is None:
        authors = []

    title_normalized = title.lower().strip()

    author_part = ""
    if authors:
        first_author = authors[0] or ""
        last_name = first_author.split()[-1].lower() if first_author else ""
        author_part = last_name

    content = f"{title_normalized}|{author_part}"
    hash_value = hashlib.sha256(content.encode()).hexdigest()[:16]
    return f"hash:{hash_value}"
@

\subsection{arXiv IDs and DOIs}

We treat arXiv identifiers as a special case because arXiv URLs are common in
metadata, and arXiv provides a canonical DOI form that many other providers
also use: [[10.48550/arXiv.<id>]].

We extract the arXiv identifier from common URL shapes:
\begin{description}
\item[abs] [[https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.12345v1]]
\item[pdf] [[https://arxiv.org/pdf/2401.12345v1.pdf]]
\item[old-style] [[https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9901001v2]]
\end{description}

We strip the version suffix (e.g., [[v1]]), because the canonical DOI is
versionless.

<<utils functions>>=
_ARXIV_URL_RE = re.compile(
    r"(?:https?://)?(?:www\.)?arxiv\.org/(?P<kind>abs|pdf)/(?P<id>[^?#]+)",
    flags=re.IGNORECASE,
)


def arxiv_id_from_url(url: str | None) -> str | None:
    """Extract a versionless arXiv id from an arXiv URL."""
    if not url:
        return None

    m = _ARXIV_URL_RE.search(url)
    if not m:
        return None

    raw = (m.group("id") or "").strip()
    if not raw:
        return None

    # PDF URLs may end with ".pdf".
    if raw.lower().endswith(".pdf"):
        raw = raw[:-4]

    # Strip version suffix, e.g. "2401.12345v2" -> "2401.12345".
    raw = re.sub(r"v\d+$", "", raw, flags=re.IGNORECASE)

    return raw or None


def arxiv_doi_from_url(url: str | None) -> str | None:
    """Return canonical arXiv DOI for an arXiv URL, if possible."""
    arxiv_id = arxiv_id_from_url(url)
    if not arxiv_id:
        return None
    return f"10.48550/arXiv.{arxiv_id}"


def derive_arxiv_doi(paper: Any) -> str | None:
    """Derive an arXiv DOI for a paper-like object.

    Only returns a DOI when the object currently has no DOI.
    """
    if getattr(paper, "doi", None):
        return None

    for candidate in (
        getattr(paper, "url", None),
        getattr(paper, "pdf_url", None),
    ):
        doi = arxiv_doi_from_url(candidate)
        if doi:
            return doi

    return None
@

