\section{Cleaning provider text}
\label{sec:clean-provider-text}

Providers hand over titles and abstracts with the markup of their own
systems still in them: HTML entities ([[&apos;]], [[&amp;]]) and inline
tags ([[<i>]]) from DBLP, OpenAlex and Web of Science, and the mojibake
of UTF-8 decoded as cp1252 or Latin-1 (an en dash arriving as
\enquote{â} plus two control characters). Every consumer---the TUI, the
notes, BibTeX entries, the audit table---would otherwise have to undo
this, so it is undone once, at ingest, by [[clean_paper_text]]; the
\LaTeX{} escapers call [[clean_metadata_text]] as well, for sessions
recorded before this existed. The mojibake repair re-encodes and decodes
and keeps the result only when the round trip succeeds, so genuine
accented text is never touched, and the tag pattern names the inline
tags explicitly so that a title such as \enquote{$x < y$ and $a > b$}
keeps its angle brackets. The marker tuple is written with [[\u]]
escapes because this file is woven into a pdf\LaTeX{} document.

One consequence is deliberate: a paper without a DOI is identified by a
hash of its title, so a record with markup in its title that was
ingested before this cleaning existed gets a new id when it is searched
again. That is the price of never storing the markup; DOI-identified
papers are unaffected.

<<utils functions>>=
import html

HTML_INLINE_TAGS = re.compile(
    r"</?\s*(?:i|b|em|strong|sup|sub|sc|scp|inf|span|tt|u)\b[^>]*>",
    re.IGNORECASE,
)
MOJIBAKE_MARKERS = ("Ã", "â", "Â")


def repair_mojibake(text: str) -> str:
    """Undo UTF-8 text that was decoded as cp1252 or Latin-1, if it was."""
    if not any(marker in text for marker in MOJIBAKE_MARKERS):
        return text
    for encoding in ("cp1252", "latin-1"):
        try:
            return text.encode(encoding).decode("utf-8")
        except (UnicodeEncodeError, UnicodeDecodeError):
            continue
    return text


def clean_metadata_text(text: str) -> str:
    """Decode entities, strip inline markup and repair mojibake."""
    text = html.unescape(text or "")
    text = HTML_INLINE_TAGS.sub("", text)
    return repair_mojibake(text)


def clean_paper_text(paper: Any) -> Any:
    """Clean the title, venue and abstract of `paper` in place."""
    for name in ("title", "venue", "abstract"):
        value = getattr(paper, name, None)
        if isinstance(value, str):
            setattr(paper, name, clean_metadata_text(value))
    return paper
@

Let's verify the three cleanings and that ordinary text survives them:

<<test functions>>=
class TestCleanProviderText:
    def test_entities_and_inline_tags(self):
        assert clean_metadata_text(
            "Developers&apos; <i>Perceptions</i> &amp; &quot;XML&quot;"
        ) == "Developers' Perceptions & \"XML\""
        assert clean_metadata_text("x < y and a > b") == "x < y and a > b"

    def test_mojibake_round_trips(self):
        assert clean_metadata_text("Thinking â Developing") \
            == "Thinking – Developing"
        assert clean_metadata_text("Thinking â€“ Developing") \
            == "Thinking – Developing"
        assert clean_metadata_text("Café résumé") \
            == "Café résumé"

    def test_clean_paper_text_in_place(self):
