\section{Contact email for polite API pools}
\label{sec:contact-email}

Several of the services Scholar talks to ask clients to identify themselves
with an email address.  OpenAlex and Crossref reward it with a faster
\enquote{polite pool}; Unpaywall (\cref{unpaywall-module}) refuses requests
without one.  Historically each integration read its own variable
([[OPENALEX_EMAIL]], [[CROSSREF_MAILTO]]), which meant a user had to discover
and set a new variable for every service even though the answer---\enquote{how
can this service reach me?}---is the same each time.

We therefore introduce one generic setting, [[SCHOLAR_EMAIL]], and a single
resolver that every integration calls.  The service-specific variables are
kept as \emph{overrides} rather than removed: an override is more specific
than the generic setting, so it wins when both are set, and existing
configurations keep working unchanged.  Centralising the precedence rule here
means no module can drift into its own ordering.

<<utils functions>>=
import os

SCHOLAR_EMAIL_VAR = "SCHOLAR_EMAIL"


def contact_email(*service_vars: str) -> str | None:
    """Return the contact email to send to an external API, or ``None``.

    A service-specific override named in ``service_vars`` (e.g.
    ``"OPENALEX_EMAIL"``) takes precedence, in the order given; otherwise
    the generic ``SCHOLAR_EMAIL`` is used.  Empty values are ignored.
    """
    for var in (*service_vars, SCHOLAR_EMAIL_VAR):
        value = os.environ.get(var, "").strip()
        if value:
            return value
    return None
@

Let's verify the precedence: the override wins, the generic setting fills in
when no override is set, and nothing set yields [[None]] rather than an empty
string (callers test truthiness to decide whether to send the parameter at
all).

<<test functions>>=
class TestContactEmail:
    """Tests for contact_email precedence."""

    def test_override_wins_over_generic(self, monkeypatch):
        monkeypatch.setenv("SCHOLAR_EMAIL", "generic@example.org")
        monkeypatch.setenv("OPENALEX_EMAIL", "specific@example.org")
        assert contact_email("OPENALEX_EMAIL") == "specific@example.org"

    def test_generic_fills_in_without_override(self, monkeypatch):
        monkeypatch.setenv("SCHOLAR_EMAIL", "generic@example.org")
        monkeypatch.delenv("OPENALEX_EMAIL", raising=False)
        assert contact_email("OPENALEX_EMAIL") == "generic@example.org"
        assert contact_email() == "generic@example.org"

    def test_nothing_set_is_none(self, monkeypatch):
        monkeypatch.delenv("SCHOLAR_EMAIL", raising=False)
        monkeypatch.delenv("CROSSREF_MAILTO", raising=False)
        assert contact_email("CROSSREF_MAILTO") is None

    def test_blank_value_is_ignored(self, monkeypatch):
        monkeypatch.setenv("SCHOLAR_EMAIL", "generic@example.org")
        monkeypatch.setenv("OPENALEX_EMAIL", "   ")
        assert contact_email("OPENALEX_EMAIL") == "generic@example.org"
